  "contract": [
    "Native frame places enable bytes at stack+0x90 and PPG words at stack+0x94. Native assembler0x61da4 scans channel_count*3 bytes from the enable pointer, not only the mask-bit extent. With four channels this spans4 mask bytes plus8 live PPG bytes.",
    "A single52-byte C struct holds enabled[4] then ppg[12], with compile-time offset/size assertions. enable_flg points to the complete object byte view, not a standalone four-byte array.",
    "Keep PPG and mask in the same live object: integrity writes into the first PPG words must immediately affect the later enable-prefix reads. Copying a12-byte prefix would not preserve this relationship.",
    "Existing packing, status gates, publication and finite rounding remain unchanged. Direct cases compare prefix content and enforce aliasing after a temporary PPG write/restoration. Dispatcher cases enforce adjacency/prefix content while running all five real frame adapters."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The original separate arrays put gain bytes after the mask in the tested Clang object; previous four-byte pointer-extent checks missed this consumer dependency. The old compiled object is retained and rejected by the new independent layout oracle.",
    "4433 native/C pairs comprise1044 direct and3389 dispatcher cases. All380 existing adapter/report instruction bytes and74 reused round bytes execute;81 direct and10 integrated selected faults match. No additional stock function is admitted.",
    "The assembler, decoder and other calculation stages remain unimplemented/modelled in these fixtures. This establishes the packet layout and alias contract, not complete computation, hardware concurrency, actual sampling or final startup/placement.",
    "All901 units compile/compose without failures or duplicate strong symbols.890 other nongenerated source/object pairs are unchanged; imports remain91 application/22 boot. Source-plan/cache files remain unchanged. Relocatable composition is not a bootable image."
  ],
